{=1}If I'm hesitating,
I should buy a lot.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:07.960
{=1}If I'm hesitating,
I should buy a lot.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:08.010
{=1}If I'm hesitating,
I should buy a lot.

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:08.050
{=1}If I'm hesitating,
I should buy a lot.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:08.090
{=1}If I'm hesitating,
I should buy a lot.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:08.130
{=1}If I'm hesitating,
I should buy a lot.

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:08.170
{=1}If I'm hesitating,
I should buy a lot.

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:11.690
I wonder if squad member
Minori is doing okay.

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:13.940
Serara didn't come, either?

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:18.270
She went to gather
ingredients with Nyan-ta.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:21.850
I wonder if she's doing okay, too.

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:23.310
Bodarel Wasteland...

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:24.100
Hm?

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:25.560
This is my first time coming here.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:28.650
Bodarel Wasteland

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:28.650
Japan Server

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:29.310
So this is around Ryogoku
in our old world, huh?

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:32.600
Seriously, I'm pretty busy, you know!

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:35.730
I'm so popular that
I have so many things to do!

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:38.560
Oh, don't talk like that,
Tetora my ma--, I mean, Baby.

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:41.190
Ms. Tetora. Isn't the
enemy showing up yet?

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:44.350
I said to call me Tetora Baby!

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:45.290
Tetora Baby.

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.650
Teto-Teto!

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:48.020
Oh, how accommodating.

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:49.980
Well, today, leave everything

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:54.020
to me, the sparking galaxy-style
goddess starlet Tetora Baby!

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:54.800
Okay!

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.270
Oh, great reply!

00:15:56.270 --> 00:15:57.850
I am hungry.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.600
We just got here! Okay, call the roll!

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:01.350
<i>Ichi!</i>

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:02.350
<i>Zwei!</i>

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:03.520
Three!

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:04.250
Hiss!

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:05.730
Hiss!

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:09.770
Okay, then!
You'll fight Hill Giants today.

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:12.440
Oh no... Seriously...?

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:12.950
Excuse me!

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.270
Yes, Toya?

00:16:14.270 --> 00:16:16.020
Giants are big!

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.230
Correct!

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:21.900
You'll start fighting more
and more big enemies soon!

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:22.910
Is that right?

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:25.650
You do have raid experiences,
too, you know!

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:28.810
That's right.
Strong enemies are usually big.

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:31.480
It's the law of bosses equal huge.

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:32.220
I see.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.020
I can't wait to fight them.

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:36.900
So today is your first step towards it.

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:40.560
Oh, by the way,
I'm not using the Teacher System

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:43.350
because it even reduces my sparkling.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:45.730
All right then! Hold on a minute, okay?

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:57.520
Okay! Begin your training now!

00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:58.240
What?!

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.600
Already?!

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:04.810
This is Pull and Slash, a common training
method used by leading Guilds.

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:07.060
Anyway, newbies just need
to fight lots of enemies.

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:09.600
And I'll use Pacification on me!

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:13.980
What? You're reducing the
hostility level just for yourself?

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:15.440
They're coming this way!

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:16.850
H-Here they come!

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:19.600
Okay, then! I'll go get the next batch!

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:22.100
Samurai's Challenge!

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:27.480
Orb of Lava!

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.190
Serpent Bolt!

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:31.560
Shoot! There are so many
I can't beat them fast enough.

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:34.270
Hold on a sec! What am I gonna do?
What am I gonna do?

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:36.980
Ahh! I hate naked people!

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:41.900
Go Away Kick! Stay Away Punch!

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:44.980
This totally has nothing
to do with my scales grudge!

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:47.770
Okay, next! Right this way, please!

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.190
Then how about this?

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:53.600
Let's see... The left one is
a Cherry Tree Twig Hitokata.

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:56.650
It strengthens the amount
of damage blocking itself.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:59.560
And the right one is a
Princess Goldfish Hitokata.

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:03.310
It extends the range of
damage blocking spells... was it?

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:05.810
Correct! Good job!

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.650
Minori. Are you having fun?

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:15.480
Of course! Thanks to your lecture,
I'm rapidly gaining knowledge!

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:17.400
Is that right? I'm glad to hear that.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:20.980
This was refreshing. I haven't felt
this way for a while. Thank you.

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:24.600
Not at all! I should be thanking you!

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:28.600
You paid for all the items
for me in the end.

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:32.230
Don't mention it. It's strange
to call it my congratulation gift to you,

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:35.480
but I'm glad that you've
become interested in raids, so...

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:39.900
In any case, when there are so
many items like this, it makes me think

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:42.690
about which item I should use when.

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:46.600
I feel like I may not use them after all,
thinking I don't wanna waste them.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.400
It's hard...

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:50.480
Don't worry.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.270
Items will tell you when to use them.

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:57.940
If you wish to win,
you'll know when to use them.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.310
I'm sure of it.

00:19:00.310 --> 00:19:01.480
Okay!

